#+TITLE: DXF/DWG writers ignore the requested version
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: enhancement
#+DEPENDS:

DXF/DWG writers ignore the requested version

== Symptom ==

write-drawing accepts a :version (a DXF $ACADVER keyword such as :ac1032 for
DWG 2018, :ac1027 for 2013) and the default-format machinery
(SAVEFORMAT / CLAUTOLISPDEFAULTDRAWINGFORMAT, 2.2.83–2.2.84) selects one, but
the codecs do not honour it:

- clautolisp/drawing/source/dxf.lisp: dxf-write-drawing /
  dxf-write-binary-drawing `(declare (ignore version))`.
- clautolisp/drawing-dwg/source/codec.lisp: dwg-write-drawing
  `(declare (ignore version))` — "the DWG version is taken from the
  DXF/libredwg defaults for now".

So the container axis (DXF-ascii / DXF-binary / DWG) is honoured but the
version is only RECORDED (on the drawing and, for DXF, the $ACADVER header):
choosing DWG 2013 vs DWG 2018 does not change the emitted geometry.

Greppable: `grep -rnE "STUB:" clautolisp/drawing*/source/`.

== Upgrade path (lightest → heaviest) ==

1. DXF ASCII: emit the version-appropriate $ACADVER and gate the
   version-specific header variables / class records; drop entity groups a
   target version predates. Mostly header + validation work.
2. Binary DXF: same, over the binary sentinel writer.
3. DWG: pass the target version to libredwg's writer (dwg_write_file takes a
   version); verify which versions the vendored libredwg build supports.

== Notes ==

When resolved, delete the STUB markers in the two codec files and replace
them with a normal note, and move this entry to the issue's Resolved tail.
Split out from issues/closed/saveformat-default-drawing-format.issue.
